{
  "id": "k8s-imagepull-typo",
  "title": "Staging rollout times out: deployment image tag v1.8.O (letter O) does not exist",
  "description": "Push to main of the squash-merged release PR #317 bumps web-frontend to 1.8.0. In k8s/deployment.yaml the pod label says 1.8.0 but the image tag was typed as v1.8.O (capital letter O instead of zero). kubectl apply succeeds and kubeconform validation passed, so the failed step only shows 'kubectl rollout status ... error: timed out waiting for the condition'. The decisive evidence is in the always() Diagnostics step that runs after it: the new pod is in ImagePullBackOff and kubelet reports 'Failed to pull image \"ghcr.io/example-org/web:v1.8.O\": ... not found'. release.yml publishes images as ghcr.io/example-org/web:<git tag>, so the intended tag is v1.8.0. The HPA FailedGetResourceMetric warnings are a side effect of the unready pod, not a cause. Fix: correct the tag in k8s/deployment.yaml. Category configuration (deploy manifest); code is also acceptable since the bad value was introduced by the change itself.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "web-frontend"
  },
